#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to preview blog posts locally using the Roq-based dev server: blog-preview.sh detects your changed posts and opens them automatically in your default browser; serve-noguides.sh starts the server only, for when you prefer to navigate to the URL yourself.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: name
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "building-blog"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Building Blog Posts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supported Platforms"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This workflow is supported on Linux, macOS, and Windows through WSL2.\n"
"Java 21+ is required. The repository includes a `./mvnw` wrapper — no\n"
"separate Maven install is needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quick Start"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run the full preview pipeline in one command — starts the Roq dev\n"
"server, waits for it to be ready, detects which posts you changed, and\n"
"opens the right URLs in your browser:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "just blog-preview\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "Or directly:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "bash blog-preview.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "To start the dev server without the auto-open behaviour:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "./serve-noguides.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then browse to [http://localhost:8042/blog/](http://localhost:8042/blog/).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:42
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "How It Works"
msgstr "仕組み"

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The site is built with [Quarkus Roq](https://docs.quarkiverse.io/quarkus-roq/dev/index.html),\n"
"a Quarkus-based static site generator. `./mvnw quarkus:dev` starts a\n"
"live-reload dev server — edits to content files are picked up\n"
"automatically without a server restart.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:52
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`blog-preview.sh` starts the dev server in the background, waits for\n"
"it to be ready (up to 300 seconds), then detects recently changed posts\n"
"and opens the right URLs in your browser. Press Ctrl-C to stop.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "Detect and Open"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "The script auto-detects what you were working on and opens the right page:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:63
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Changed posts | Preview URLs |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| 1 post | `/blog/` (listing) + `/blog/<slug>/` (deep-link) |\n"
"| 2–4 posts | `/blog/` (listing) + a tab for each post |\n"
"| 5+ posts | `/blog/` (listing only), unless git narrows it |\n"
"| No changes | `/blog/` (listing only) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:66
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The slug is derived from the filename: strip the `YYYY-MM-DD-` prefix\n"
"and the file extension (`.adoc`, `.asciidoc`, or `.md`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:70
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Change detection uses a `.blog-preview-last-run` timestamp file on\n"
"repeat runs, and falls back to `git diff`/`git log` on first run.\n"
"Delete `.blog-preview-last-run` to reset.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "Profiles"
msgstr "プロファイル"

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:78
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Script | Profile | What it includes |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| `./serve.sh` | (default) | Full site with all guides |\n"
"| `./serve-noguides.sh` | `noguides` | Site without guides (fast) |\n"
"| `./serve-only-latest-guides.sh` | `only-latest-guides` | Site with latest + main guides |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "For blog-only work, `serve-noguides.sh` is the fastest option.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blog Post File Conventions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "Location: `content/posts/YYYY-MM-DD-slug.adoc` (or `.asciidoc`, `.md`)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "Front matter fields: `layout: post`, `title`, `tags`, `synopsis`, `author`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "`author` must match a key in `_data/authors.yaml`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tags: lowercase, space-separated — e.g. `tags: extension kafka`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:89
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Images: store in `public/assets/images/posts/<slug>/`, reference with\n"
"`:imagesdir: /assets/images/posts/<slug>`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "Future-Dated Posts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:94
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Posts with a `date` value in the future are served normally by the\n"
"local dev server. No special flag or workaround is needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "Iteration Loop"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "Edit content/posts/YYYY-MM-DD-slug.adoc (or .asciidoc / .md) → save → Roq rebuilds → browser refreshes\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:103
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quarkus dev mode watches for file changes and triggers an incremental\n"
"rebuild automatically.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:104
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr "トラブルシューティング"

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:114
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Port already in use** — Both `blog-preview.sh` and `./serve-noguides.sh`\n"
"default to port 8042.\n"
"First, check whether it is a leftover preview from a previous run\n"
"(e.g. a `java` process launched by `mvnw`). If so, kill it and retry.\n"
"**Always tell the user before using a different port** — do not\n"
"silently switch ports without informing them. If the conflict cannot\n"
"be resolved, ask the user which port to use, then set the environment\n"
"variable:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:115
#, no-wrap
msgid "QUARKUS_HTTP_PORT=8081 bash blog-preview.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "or for the bare server:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "QUARKUS_HTTP_PORT=8081 ./serve-noguides.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:128
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Changes not appearing** — Quarkus dev mode watches source files. If a\n"
"change is not picked up, press `s` in the terminal running the dev\n"
"server to force a restart, or stop and re-run `./serve-noguides.sh`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:133
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Post not appearing** — Check that the file is in `content/posts/`\n"
"with the correct `YYYY-MM-DD-slug.adoc` (or `.asciidoc`, `.md`)\n"
"naming and that the front matter `layout: post` and `author` fields\n"
"are present and valid.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:136
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Slow first start** — The first run downloads Maven dependencies.\n"
"Subsequent starts are fast.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:141
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`blog-preview.sh` exits with \"Server process exited unexpectedly\"**\n"
"— Maven started but then died. Scroll up in the terminal to find the\n"
"build error. Common causes: corrupted local Maven repository, a\n"
"missing or broken dependency, or a compile error in the project.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md:145
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`blog-preview.sh` exits with \"neither mvnw nor mvn found\"** — The\n"
"`./mvnw` wrapper is missing or not executable. Run `chmod +x mvnw`\n"
"to restore it. Do not attempt to install Maven system-wide — the\n"
"wrapper is the correct entry point for this project.\n"
msgstr ""
